  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 2.1.1, package.json says 2.0.2.",
        "  The App Store and the server read info.xml; everything on the node side reads package.json. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying two version numbers, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml states no <repository>.",
        "  <repository> is the only machine-readable link from a published release back to the source it was built from, and <bugs> is where the App Store page sends a report. Without them a user of the release has no way back to the project."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "script-without-config",
      "lines": [
        "composer.json scripts cs:check, cs:fix call php-cs-fixer, and no PHP-CS-Fixer configuration is in the checkout.",
        "  php-cs-fixer fix --dry-run --diff",
        "  The command is there to be run, so whoever runs it gets a tool that has nothing to go by - and CI, if it runs the script, reports the failure as the change under test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "The licence is stated differently: agpl (appinfo/info.xml, package.json), GPL-3.0-or-later (composer.json).",
        "  Whoever redistributes the app has to pick one of them, and the App Store shows the one from info.xml.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  No SPDX id: agpl (package.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is sendentsynchroniser, the checkout directory is Sendent-Synchroniser-App-for-Nextcloud.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "link-redirect",
      "lines": [
        "A link of appinfo/info.xml has moved permanently:",
        "  <website> https://www.sendent.com",
        "    now https://sendent.com/",
        "  The old address works only as long as the redirect is kept; the new one can be stated directly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 28 to 35; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 28 reaches below the oldest maintained major (32), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 22 stated in lint.yml, release.yml, static.yml, within package.json engines.node >=20.",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.js, superseded form), Stylelint (stylelint.config.js), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (phpunit.xml).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.js: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No PHP-CS-Fixer configuration: no coding standard is applied to the PHP sources, so formatting is settled in review instead of by a command.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "1 declared package is named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/vue.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 120 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3) in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines).",
        "  make reads GNUmakefile and never Makefile; it runs only with make -f <name>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "Every directory the shipped PHP reaches through __DIR__ and the frontend through linkTo is in the shipped file set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk)."
      ]
    }
  ],
